From 3f2c941e122a6306afe36f271308b828c41c14af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Juuso Alasuutari <juuso.alasuutari@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 09:53:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] composition: add the native transport, HDR handling and
 pass cleanup

This commit changes the composition for dlsslop-amd's native daemon and
the in-layer network:
- the proxy and answer can live in device-local memory that is exported
  to the daemon, with queue family ownership transfers at every leg;
- display-encoded FP16 proxies, PQ (HDR10) decoding and BT.2020 to
  BT.709 conversion, without adding negative BT.709 coordinates;
- the model raster keeps the low-resolution source and answer together;
- write-only storage images are formatless;
- dlssnr_pass and scaler_vk write their descriptor sets on every
  dispatch. Before this commit, a per-slot cache skipped writes when a
  slot's inputs looked unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
